Loopback files are files that can contian a filesystem itself and these files cna be mounted similary to a physical device.

sudo dd if=/dev/zero of=juck.data bs=1M count=1

dd is command which work's at very low level in the device.


Loopback are the filesystems those that we create in files rather than a physcial device.

Making a `Loopback` 
------------------

sudo dd if=/dev/zeros of=lookbackfile.img bs=1G count=1

mkfs.ext4 loopbackfile.img

sudo mkdir -p /mnt/loopback

mount -o loop lookbackfile.img /mnt/loopback

-o loop is used to mount lookback filesytem

Manual SetUp
------------

losetup /dev/loop1 lookbackfile.img

sudo mount /dev/loop1 /mnt/loopback

unmout /mnt/loopback


